pan> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"A block of the source string `s`, with its inline content parsed.","docLink":"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.Block","kind":"inductive","line":236,"name":"Lean.Markdown.Block","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.lean#L236-L253"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.ListKind.sameKind\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Markdown</span>.<span class=\"name\">ListKind</span>.<span class=\"name\">sameKind</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.ListKind\">ListKind</a> → <a href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.ListKind\">ListKind</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether two list kinds belong to the same list (that is, they have matching marker styles).\n\nThe starting number of an ordered list is irrelevant, so `1.` and `5.` are the same list kind.\nBullets must use the exact same character, and ordered lists must use the same delimiter.","docLink":"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.ListKind.sameKind","kind":"def","line":223,"name":"Lean.Markdown.ListKind.sameKind","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.lean#L223-L232"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Data/Markdown/Block.html#Lean.Markdown.Block.instInhabitedRaw\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Markdown</span>.<s